{
  "source": "Made by scripts/make_libero_scene.py from text files read on 2026-11-14; nothing of LIBERO runs to make it and no file was executed or unpickled. objects.*.boxes, density, friction and contain: the type=\"box\" collision geoms and the contain_region site of LIBERO's object XML files (libero/libero/assets/stable_hope_objects/<kind>/<kind>.xml and libero/libero/assets/stable_scanned_objects/basket/basket.xml, github.com/Lifelong-Robot-Learning/LIBERO, MIT licence), in metres in the object's own frame, numbers as written there except that every box quaternion is normalized as MuJoCo does when it compiles a model (butter's, cream cheese's and bbq sauce's are not unit in the XML); the mesh scale of an XML applies to its visual mesh only. objects.*.quat: the orientation LIBERO gives the object's free joint, from each class's rotation and rotation_axis (libero/libero/envs/objects/hope_objects.py, google_scanned_objects.py) passed through TableRegionSampler._sample_quat (libero/libero/envs/regions/workspace_region_sampler.py) and written unconverted to qpos by BDDLBaseDomain._reset_internal (libero/libero/envs/bddl_base_domain.py); LIBERO draws no yaw for these objects. objects.*.z, height and footprint: computed here from the corners of the boxes turned by quat, with the lowest corner on the floor; they are not LIBERO numbers. libero_sites: the bottom_site, top_site and horizontal_radius_site positions of each XML and the height LIBERO's sampler drops the object frame at (0.01 - 0.035 - bottom_site z, floor plane at z = 0); those sites are rough placeholders, not the objects' real extents. tasks: the ten LIBERO-Object tasks, keyed by the kind of the object to pick, each from its three BDDL files: libero/libero/bddl_files/libero_object/<name>.bddl in LIBERO (variant original) and, in LIBERO-PRO (Zhou et al., arXiv:2510.03827; code MIT, data CC BY 4.0; Hugging Face dataset zhouxueyang/LIBERO-Pro), bddl_files/libero_object_swap/<name>.bddl (variant swap) and bddl_files/07_initial_pose_position_angle/bddl/libero_object/<name>.bddl (variant pose: the target's region centre plus its delta_xy, and its yaw); task repeats tasks.alphabet_soup. Every xy is a region centre in this sim's frame, which is LIBERO's floor frame moved by +0.6 m in x because LIBERO stands its Panda base at (-0.6, 0, 0) (OnTheGroundPanda.base_xpos_offset[\"empty\"]) and this sim has it at the origin; reach is the distance from that origin to the variant's target, computed here. placement: for each kind, the half-width in metres of the square LIBERO really draws the object's centre in, around its region's centre: TableRegionSampler keeps ensure_object_boundary_in_range=True, so MultiRegionRandomSampler._sample_x and _sample_y (libero/libero/envs/regions/base_region_sampler.py) draw between min + r and max - r with r the x of the XML's horizontal_radius_site, which is |side / 2 - r| either side of the centre, computed here for the 5 cm object regions and, for the basket, its 2 cm bin_region; where r exceeds side / 2 the bounds cross and numpy's uniform still draws between them.",
